---
description: Check if current pitch is ready for development and move it to ready/
---

This gate VERIFIES; it does not investigate, decide, or edit the pitch. Shaping already ran the Pitch Readiness Check, the inline probe discipline, and every blocker scan — `/ready` re-confirms none of that has gone stale and refuses on any gap. It never repairs: no resolve-by-investigation loop, no auto-written `## Decisions` rows, no `AskUserQuestion` on a contradicted or inconclusive claim. A gap found here means the pitch goes back to shaping, not forward through a second gate that does shaping's job for it.

**1. Structural scan** — read the pitch currently in scope and confirm, structurally, ALL of:

- Frontmatter present with `status: SHAPED`, non-empty `scope:`, and `summary:`.
- A `## Claim ledger` section with ZERO `UNPROBED` rows, zero proxy rows (a probe that reads/describes instead of EXERCISING the contract), and zero rows whose claim is the pitch's OWN proposed work (a ledger row states a claim about reality AS IT EXISTS NOW, falsifiable independent of whether this pitch ships — the pitch's own unbuilt move belongs in `## Problem`/`## Solution sketch`, never in the ledger, `UNPROBED` or otherwise).
- Every ledger row's probe command appears, verbatim, as a `$ <command>` + fenced output transcript in `## References`.
- A `## Decisions` section with a row for every `Assumed:` appearing in the pitch's own prose (`ID | Decision | Why | Source | Consequence`).
- No `## Questions` block remaining (an orphan `## Answers` with no `## Questions` is fine — it means questions were resolved and headings deleted).
- No fork phrasing anywhere in the title or Solution sketch: "X or Y", "route or delete", "either/or", "TBD", "decide at build", "investigate at build", "investigate on review", "verify during build".
- SWEEP-CLASS COMPLETENESS: if the pitch is a purge/sweep/audit/collapse/rename/remove operation, `## References` carries a full-vocabulary sweep transcript (grep against committed state) AND a producer/verifier reconciliation. Either missing → NOT ready.
- Latent contract-mirror fork: if the pitch mirrors/extends/ports/clones an existing launcher, command, function, or role, `## References` carries a contract-read of the target (positional/required args, `"$@"` passthrough, output format, exit codes). Missing → NOT ready.
- External-contract table (when present) uses ONLY the closed disposition vocabulary `{Preserved, Dropped, Unchanged, REMOVED, BREAKING}` — a hand-invented label is a structural gap. A `BREAKING` row carries a `## Decisions` entry recording the forced-break justification.
- Every `## Related pitches` / cross-reference resolves to a file on disk in `codegen/pitches/{draft,ready,shipped}/` (the same-motivation Rabbit-hole/No-go carve-out is exempt — it deliberately carries no draft reference).
- A spike brief (when the pitch's core value is a novel cross-system mechanism) has every row naming a measurement and carrying an embedded transcript, with the negative control ordered first.

Any gap → **refuse**: name the specific gap and the pitch section that owns it as a structured `{gap, owning_section}` pair, leave the file in `draft/`. Do not edit the pitch to close the gap — this gate still never repairs. Hand the refusal back per the **Refusal hand-off** contract below rather than stopping here.

**2. Staleness re-run** — for every ledger row, re-execute its recorded probe command VERBATIM (delegate read-only re-runs through `codegen-call` per the delegated-enumeration rule when the re-run set spans more than one file; transcribe, never interpret) and diff the fresh output against the row's recorded Outcome.

- Match → row stands, continue.
- Drift → **refuse**: name the row, the recorded Outcome, and the fresh output. Do not auto-decide, do not edit the pitch, do not raise `AskUserQuestion`. The pitch goes back to shaping to reconcile the drift.

**3. Handoff reconciliation** (run once steps 1–2 are clean): if the pitch's frontmatter carries a `handoffs:` list (a bilateral cross-pitch deferral record — see `codegen/pitches/draft/deferred-work-has-exactly-one-owner.md`), run `cd "$ROOT/test_harness" && MIX_BUILD_PATH=_build/pitch_scope_parity mix codegen.pitches.scope --check --dir=draft --cwd="$ROOT" --slug=<slug> --stamp-handoff-receipt` (resolve `$ROOT` the same way as **Move** below, first). A HANDOFF GAP failure (missing counterpart, mismatched record copy, or an owner not listing the path in its own `scope:`) means the pitch is NOT ready — name the exact gap (usually: add the identical record to the counterpart pitch, or add the path to the owner's `scope:`) and refuse. A clean run mints/refreshes `handoff_receipt:` in every draft participant; nothing else changes. A pitch with no `handoffs:` key is unaffected — this step is a no-op for it.

**4. Commit-subject seal check**: every pitch reaching `ready/` MUST carry a `commit_subject:` frontmatter field that passes `codegen-commit --check-subject "<text>"`. Missing or mechanically invalid → **refuse**, name the check failure (length, casing, trailing period, trailer token). Do not derive or rewrite the subject here — that is shaping's job (see `shape.txt`'s "On completion" step).

**Move** (only when steps 1–4 are ALL clean): move the draft to `ready/` at the DURABLE main-repo root (a `/ready` issued from an experiment session must act on the main-repo pitch, not an ephemeral worktree copy). Resolve the root first: `ROOT="${CODEGEN_PITCH_ROOT:-$(cd "$(dirname "$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir 2>/dev/null)")" 2>/dev/null && pwd || pwd)}"`. Then `mkdir -p "$ROOT/codegen/pitches/ready"` and `mv "$ROOT/codegen/pitches/draft/<slug>.md" "$ROOT/codegen/pitches/ready/<slug>.md"`. (Plain `mv`, not `git mv` — pitch files are untracked and never committed, so `git mv` would fail because git has no record of the source file.)

**Before move to ready/**: Emit end-summary in chat —

1.  **What the change consists of** — the concrete edit surface.
2.  **How it affects the system** — which consumers, contexts, modules are touched.
3.  **How it affects users** — observable behavior change.
    Call out every **assumed default** explicitly: `Assumed: <dimension> = <default> (override if wrong)`. This includes every auto-decide blocker resolution already recorded in `## Decisions`.

Report: "READY. Moved to ready/."

**If not ready**: report `NOT READY: <gap> — <owning section>.` The file stays in `draft/`. Do not investigate the gap, do not edit the pitch, do not raise `AskUserQuestion` — this gate never repairs.

**Refusal hand-off**: when `/ready` is invoked BY the shaper itself (the normal case — shaping invokes `/ready` on its own completion, never stops and waits to be told per `shape.txt`), a refusal is the input to a NEW shaping-loop iteration on the SAME gap, closed there, then `/ready` is re-invoked. Three stop conditions end the loop and surface to the operator instead of looping further: the SAME gap reported twice in a row; a genuine product-fork decision (routes to the ASK-GATE below, never auto-decided here); a 3-round ceiling on `/ready` invocations for one pitch. When `/ready` is invoked directly by the operator (not via a live shaping session), report the refusal and stop — there is no shaping loop to hand back to.

**ASK-GATE: product forks only** — this gate raises no questions and makes no product-fork decisions; the ASK-GATE governs shaping, not verification. A gap needing a product-fork decision is one of the three stop conditions above, not something this gate resolves.

